		<meta property="schema:abstract">Apologia Pro Vita Sua is Newman’s history of his religious opinions, from his childhood to his reception into the Catholic Church in 1845.</meta>
		<dc:description>
			&lt;p&gt;Apologia Pro Vita Sua is Newman’s history of his religious opinions, from his childhood to his reception into the Catholic Church in 1845. He wrote it in 1864 in reply to Charles Kingsley, who had charged him with indifference to truth. This edition has a preface, five chapters, seven notes, supplemental matter and eight additional notes.&lt;/p&gt;
		</dc:description>
